  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "There are a number of features that are important for",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "supporting ingest and export of objects. These are:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1. Ingest SIP (self-contained) - This would be for a",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "single digital object, that there is the ability for",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "all datastream content to be inlined or attached so",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "that it is not necessary for the repository to call",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "back to obtain the content bytestream.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2. Ingest Archive - This would be a whole set of",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "self-contained SIPS bound together as an archive that",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "can be ingested into the repository in an efficient manner.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3. Export (self-contained) - This would be an export",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "of a single digital object where the content of all",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "managed content datastreams is inlined or attached. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "This can enable a dump and load of a repository since",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "this export can file become a self-contained SIP (as in",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "#1) above. This allows you to dump a Fedora",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "repository, shut it down, and still be able to load up",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "a new repository using the export files as SIPS -",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "without having to do callbacks to the original",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "repository to get the managed content datastreams.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "4. Export Archive - This would be a whole set of",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "self-contained export files bound together as an archive.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Date: 2006-11-15 10:01",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Sender: payette",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Logged In: YES ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "user_id=128",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Ingest/Export (self-contained objects) is complete (#1 and #3).",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Ingest/Export archive of many objects is a future item.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Date: 2005-11-16 11:27",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Sender: payette",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Logged In: YES ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "user_id=128",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Need to look at options for self-contained SIP ingest:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1) base64 inlining",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) SOAP attachments",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) XOP",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "4) ARC files",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "5) other",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Date: 2005-11-16 11:25",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Sender: payette",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Logged In: YES ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "user_id=128",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "More comments on the problem:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Now, the object export will create \"public\" callback",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "URLs",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "for datastreams of type M (managed content). This",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "works well for migration (export from one repository and",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "ingest into new repository) as long as the old repository",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "is up and running at the time of the ingest into the new",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "repository. Then the datastream content can be",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "sucked into the new repository via callback URLs",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(getItem requests on default disseminator).",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "However, if the old repository is not available after an",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "export, or if you just want to dump and re-load the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "SAME repository we need a way to get the managed",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "content out of the repository as part of the export.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "In the Fedora spec, we envisioned a variant of the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "export file with base-64 encoded binary content inlined",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "for the managed content datastreams. Then, the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "export file is complete in that it has all the datastream",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "content that was in the repository within it.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "We can either create another export method on API-M",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "such as exportWithContent() or parameterize the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "existing export method. From the ingest standpoint, we",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
